 ### TensoRF
-A tensor-based radiance field representation that decomposes the 3D scene into low-rank factors, offering memory efficiency compared to dense grids. AReT uses a VM-rank-16 configuration [S1, unofficial].
+A tensor-based radiance field representation that decomposes the 3D scene into low-rank factors, offering memory efficiency compared to dense grids [G]. AReT uses a VM-rank-16 configuration. Choose when memory constraints limit dense grid storage and low-rank factorization is acceptable for the target resolution [G]. [TensoRF](13550-model-architecture-and-encoding.md)
 
 ### MedNeRF
-A generative-prior-guided NeRF approach that uses a population-level latent code from a GAN. AReT outperforms MedNeRF in sparse-view settings because MedNeRF's diffuse density field and scene-agnostic thresholding degrade patient-specific accuracy [S1, unofficial].
+A generative-prior-guided NeRF approach that uses a population-level latent code from a GAN. AReT outperforms MedNeRF in sparse-view settings because MedNeRF's diffuse density field and scene-agnostic thresholding degrade patient-specific accuracy. Choose when population-level priors are acceptable and dense multi-view data is available [G]. [MedNeRF](18360-generative-and-gan-based-methods.md)
 
 ### Classical Sparse-View Methods (FDK, SART)
